# Keep line endings stable across machines.
#
# Without this, editing on Windows can rewrite whole files to CRLF, which makes
# every line look changed and buries real edits in the diff.
#
# Source and text files are stored as LF in the repo (Windows editors handle LF
# fine). The Windows batch launcher is the exception - cmd.exe needs CRLF.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

*.command text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf

# Binary assets - never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.vsix binary
